Tests of AutoSave into the document's own file (hst-user-autosave-filter.patch).

CppunitTest_sfx2_hst_autosave makes the two calls of the AutoRecovery timer (getArgs2 HstUserAutoSave, then
storeSelf with HstUserAutoSave) and checks the file on disk, the state of .uno:HstAutoSave and the questions the
document's own interaction handler receives: a .docx opens with AutoSave on and is saved in place; Undo still
works after it; .doc, .txt and .rtf are dimmed and never written, without a "Keep current format" question; an
unnamed document and a read-only one are dimmed; a .docx with Basic macros is dimmed; a file changed by another
program is not overwritten and pauses AutoSave without a dialog, a click resumes it; a removed drive pauses it
without a dialog and the document stays modified; the toggle is for the session only.

License: the new test files are HST-owned (LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary); Module_sfx2.mk keeps MPL-2.0.
Test: make CppunitTest_sfx2_hst_autosave.
